              "jcr:created": "Tue Apr 15 2025 15:47:44 GMT+0000",
              "alt": "Sepsis and non-vent hospital-acquired pneumonia: Understanding the risk, prevention and early recognition",
              "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/sage/focusrn-live/videos/Kathleen-Vollman-sepsis-webinar-thumbnail.jpg",
              "borderColor": "rgb(0,0,0)",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Oct 12 2026 20:45:49 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
              "linkInternal": "/content/stryker/us/en/sage/webinars/sepsis-non-vent-pneumonia-risk-prevention-recognition",
              "enableBorder": "true"
            },
            "text": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Thu Apr 03 2025 21:24:57 GMT+0000",
              "text": "<h4>Sepsis and non-vent hospital-acquired pneumonia: Understanding the risk, prevention and early recognition</h4>\n<p><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Kathleen Vollman MSN, RN, CCNS, FCCM, FCNS, FAAN</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">This session reviews the impact of sepsis, emerging quality initiatives, evidence-based pneumonia prevention strategies and the nurse's role in early sepsis recognition and intervention. Attendees will leave with practical strategies for addressing risk and supporting improved outcomes for hospitalized patients.<br>\n</span></p>\n<p><a href=\"/content/stryker/us/en/sage/webinars/sepsis-non-vent-pneumonia-risk-prevention-recognition.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"standalone-link\">Watch now</span></a></p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Oct 12 2026 20:47:11 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          },
          "col2": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "standaloneimage_copy": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "preset": "max_width_1440",
              "jcr:created": "Tue Apr 15 2025 15:47:44 GMT+0000",
              "alt": "Hidden in plain sight: NVHAP title card",
              "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/sage/focusrn-live/videos/318005_nv-hap-title-screen.jpg",
              "borderColor": "rgb(0,0,0)",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Tue May 26 2026 20:27:42 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
              "linkInternal": "/content/stryker/us/en/sage/webinars/nv-hap-hidden-plain-sight",
              "enableBorder": "true"
            },
            "text_copy": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "jcr:created": "Thu Apr 03 2025 21:24:57 GMT+0000",
              "text": "<h4>Hidden in plain sight: non-ventilator hospital-acquired pneumonia (NVHAP) - the #1 hospital-acquired infection</h4>\n<p><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Dian Baker PhD, MA, MS, APRN</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">This course will provide healthcare professionals with an in-depth understanding of non-ventilator hospital-acquired pneumonia (NVHAP), its clinical consequences and the role of the human lung microbiome in the development of this infection. The session will also introduce the adapted island model of the lung microbiome and explore how this model may help inform preventive measures and actionable practices to address the risk of NVHAP among critically ill patients.</span></p>\n<p><a href=\"/content/stryker/us/en/sage/webinars/nv-hap-hidden-plain-sight.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"standalone-link\">Watch now</span></a></p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Jun 03 2026 19:52:15 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          },
          "col3": {
            "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
            "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
            "standaloneimage": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "preset": "max_width_1440",
              "jcr:created": "Tue Jun 24 2025 21:31:08 GMT+0000",
              "alt": "Urinary incontinence webinar thumbnail",
              "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/sage/focusrn-live/videos/urinary-incontinence-protecting-patients-skin.jpg",
              "borderColor": "rgb(0,0,0)",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Jun 24 2025 21:33:02 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
              "linkInternal": "/content/stryker/us/en/sage/webinars/managing-urinary-incontinence-webinar",
              "enableBorder": "true"
            },
            "text_copy": {
              "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
              "jcr:createdBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-7a617b9e44@example.invalid",
              "hideComponent": "false",
              "topMargin": "4",
              "jcr:created": "Tue Jun 24 2025 21:28:10 GMT+0000",
              "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
              "text": "<h4><span class=\"futura-bold\">Making it Happen: Managing Urinary Incontinence and Protecting Patients' Skin</span></h4>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Carmen Davis MSN, RN, CCRN, CNS-BC&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">This presentation offers an overview of the prevalence, costs and risk factors of urinary incontinence (UI), incontinence-associated dermatitis (IAD), and pressure injury (PI). We will examine how one phenomenon can lead to another, along with strategies to help prevent and manage these conditions in the clinical setting. Basic physiology will be reviewed to support understanding potential etiologies and best practice treatment strategies. Change management approaches will be discussed to help our team members adopt best practices and improve patient outcomes.</span></p>\n<p><a href=\"/content/stryker/us/en/sage/webinars/managing-urinary-incontinence-webinar.html\"><span class=\"standalone-link\">Watch now</span></a></p>\n",
              "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Jun 24 2025 21:32:45 GMT+0000",
              "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
              "textIsRich": "true"
            }
          }
        }
      },
